node_modules/

# `dist*/` and not `dist/`: a failed `rm -rf dist` on macOS can leave a
# "dist 2" or "dist 3" beside it, and those are build output too — one of
# them was 23 files of a day-old build, about to be committed.
dist*/
.astro/
shots/
scripts/.fonts-cache/
chrome-headless-shell/
.DS_Store

# macOS duplicate-file artifacts. A failed copy or delete leaves "Face 2.astro"
# beside Face.astro — and the one that turned up here was the version from
# BEFORE the face-wash fix, so anyone reading it would have read the bug.
# Nothing in this project is ever meant to have a space and a digit like this.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]/

# scratch files from the no-browser visual checks (rendering the chef, the
# badges and the share card to PNG to actually look at them)
*.tmp.*
.*.tmp.*
*.log
.env
.env.*
local-preview*/

# The legal handoff note. Its own table says "No. Never publish it", and it
# lists every unfixed legal risk before launch, the App Store guidelines that
# could reject the build, and internal file paths — while the documents it
# accompanies are under a trade-secrecy rule that names no vendor anywhere.
# A public repo publishes it. It stays on disk; it does not ship.
# If the repo is ever private, delete these two lines.
legal/README.md
